+---
+id: dl-001-task-ids-are-sequential-per-list-and-a-title-wins-over-an-id
+type: decision-log
+title: "Task ids are sequential per list, and a title wins over an id"
+status: pending
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold verbatim; `memory submit` replaces
+     these placeholder comments with real content and fills the required frontmatter fields. -->
+
+## Context
+Tasks need a stable reference that survives a rename. The domain may not use the clock or randomness
+(r3), so ids cannot be UUIDs or timestamps.
+
+## Decision
+Each list numbers its tasks `task-1`, `task-2`, … with a counter that only grows, so the id of a removed
+task is never reused. Where a title is taken, a task is looked up by title first, then by id; a title
+that equals another task's id therefore keeps meaning the title.
+
+## Consequences
+Ids are unique within a list only, and deterministic. A task titled like another's id can only be
+reached by that id through `get`.
